From: Omarchy Mobile <omamobile@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] i2c: qup: refuse transfers while system suspended

qup_i2c_suspend() turns the controller's clocks off but leaves its
runtime PM status active and never tells the I2C core the adapter is
suspended. A transfer that comes after it, before qup_i2c_resume(), so
finds pm_runtime_get_sync() a no-op and touches the QUP registers with
their clocks off.

Such transfers happen: LED triggers fire from power_supply_changed()
during suspend and resume, and a leds-aw2013 brightness work then
wrote to the controller after it had suspended. On a Redmi 4 Prime
(msm8953-xiaomi-markw) that ended in

  Internal error: synchronous external abort: 0000000096000010
  Workqueue: leds set_brightness_delayed
  pc : qup_i2c_xfer_v2+0xc1c/0xcd4
   aw2013_brightness_set+0x174/0x2bc [leds_aw2013]

when it was caught, and otherwise in a bus hang that the SoC turned
into a PS_HOLD reset at almost every s2idle. With the LED triggers
detached, 10 of 10 s2idle cycles and a 300 s one resumed cleanly where
every run before had reset in its first cycle.

Mark the adapter suspended first, so the core rejects late transfers
with -ESHUTDOWN instead of reaching the hardware, and suspend and
resume through pm_runtime_force_suspend()/pm_runtime_force_resume(),
so the runtime PM status matches the clocks.

---
 drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qup.c | 16 +++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qup.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qup.c
@@ -1981,16 +1981,20 @@

 static int qup_i2c_suspend(struct device *device)
 {
-	if (!pm_runtime_suspended(device))
-		return qup_i2c_pm_suspend_runtime(device);
-	return 0;
+	struct qup_i2c_dev *qup = dev_get_drvdata(device);
+
+	i2c_mark_adapter_suspended(&qup->adap);
+	return pm_runtime_force_suspend(device);
 }

 static int qup_i2c_resume(struct device *device)
 {
-	qup_i2c_pm_resume_runtime(device);
-	pm_request_autosuspend(device);
-	return 0;
+	struct qup_i2c_dev *qup = dev_get_drvdata(device);
+	int ret;
+
+	ret = pm_runtime_force_resume(device);
+	i2c_mark_adapter_resumed(&qup->adap);
+	return ret;
 }

 static const struct dev_pm_ops qup_i2c_qup_pm_ops = {
